.TH AESBREAKER 1 "2026-11-23" "AES-Breaker 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aesbreaker \- offline AES decryption and password recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aesbreaker
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AES-Breaker recovers passwords for AES Crypt v1/v2/v3, OpenSSL enc, WinZip AES,
and explicit JSON-spec custom AES files. Results are labelled confirmed,
probable, or weak according to the format's actual verification mechanism.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B crack
Recover a password with wordlists, rules, masks, hybrids, or a combinator.
.TP
.B decrypt
Decrypt with a known password or an explicit raw AES specification.
.TP
.B inspect
Describe a container without decrypting it.
.TP
.B analyze
Entropy, duplicate-block, magic, and container checks for unknown data.
.TP
.B derive
Reproduce EVP_BytesToKey, PBKDF2, or HKDF.
.TP
.B cribdrag
Test a known plaintext crib against two CTR/OFB ciphertexts.
.TP
.B recover-iv
Recover a CBC IV or a stream keystream from known plaintext.
.TP
.B infer
Rank raw AES mode/IV interpretations with explicit confidence.
.TP
.B encrypt
Create AES Crypt v2/v3, OpenSSL enc, or WinZip AES containers.
.TP
.B selftest
Run known-answer and interoperability checks.
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B aesbreaker command --help
for the complete option list. Common long-running options include
.BR --max-runtime ,
.BR --checkpoint ,
and
.BR --resume .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success or password found.
.TP
.B 1
Password not found, no inference candidates, or selftest failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, input, format, or output error.
.TP
.B 3
Verification/decryption failure or partial extraction.
.TP
.B 124
--max-runtime limit reached.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by Ctrl-C.
.SH FILES
.I docs/formats.md
contains exact wire-format descriptions.
.I docs/custom-spec.schema.json
describes the custom spec format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl (1),
.BR 7z (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Talha Kacar.
